members.doc:
Content-Security-Policy for HTML pages, given the response's nonce (inline scripts carry it).
Default: strict nonce policy (`strictCSP`); `CSPOptions` (`{ trustedTypes, directives }`): `strictCSP` with them (directives checked at startup);
`false` sends none. A `headers()` CSP wins.

symbols.remarks:
Strict CSP: only nonce'd scripts and what they load run; no plugins, no `<base>` hijacking.
`{ trustedTypes: true }` also enforces Trusted Types (`csp: (nonce) => strictCSP(nonce, { trustedTypes: true })`);
`{ directives }` merges extra directives (`cspPolicy`).

Scoped stylesheet as a tagged template at module top level: `const s = css\`.card { … }\``.
The compiler (`rivet()` Vite plugin) replaces it with a frozen class map and extracts the CSS;
calling it at runtime means the module was not compiled with styles enabled.
